  "limitations": [
    "The database records published ratings, not the calibration state or health of a particular physical instrument.",
    "KXCI *OPT? does not identify every exact product model or every external accessory; do not infer 4201/4211, CVU variant, CVIV, GNDU wiring or interlock state from it.",
    "The SMU maximum power and range limits are conservative planning boundaries; actual output depends on source mode, selected range, load, cables, temperature and instrument condition.",
    "The PMU/PGU load equations are based on nominal 50 ohm source impedance and are approximate; verify the actual fixture and cabling.",
    "A module's output rating is not a safe operating limit for an arbitrary DUT. DUT voltage, current, power, energy, pulse width and thermal limits must be separately supplied.",
    "Pulse timing values are documented recommended minima/typical characteristics, not a guarantee of measurement accuracy for every DUT and cable configuration.",
    "The database is not a substitute for the official manuals, laboratory electrical-safety procedures or physical interlocks."
  ]
